Z||000007||Fiero2||06-05-2001||06:55 PM||||Eric, I didn't realize that the engine came with a whole car  LOL.<BR>Seems like a pretty good deal though, but we don't really need another Fiero at the moment.<BR>Anyone else have just a good 2.8 for sale?<BR>I guess it's another trip to Kick Hill. Hey 88coupeV6, what day is good for you?<P>Marian<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000008||Bozone||06-05-2001||07:36 PM||||The pictures look great. I was really unprepared for that event. I left my camera at home. I wasn't wearing my Fiero factory Swap Meet t-shirt. The car was dirty. Drats. It's clean now though.  Anyway, glad you had a camera Steve.<P>Bozone, eeeeeh, Mr. Potatohead whatever! :-) ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero5||06-05-2001||08:19 PM||||Boomtastic wrote: "I think you need one with more 'grunt'!"<P>Eric, that is the loudest 4 cyl growling out of the dual exhaust with GT cones I have ever heard! I don't think it needs anymore "grunt!" Maybe a little more oomph, but deffinately not anymore grunt. Yeesh!<P>Steve ||||reg||12
Z||000010||Phil||06-05-2001||08:44 PM||||I have to agree with Fred, Bozone, Mr. Potato Head, or whatever he is calling himself today.  Thanks, Steve and Josh, for remembering your cameras and posting your pictures of The Fiore Pontiac show.  The pictures are great.  So glad that it turned out to be a nice day after all.  We enjoyed having everyone who could make it come back to our house after the show.    <P>Phil & Gwen||||reg||1
